the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for *a case*.
    the answer to Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r4_12_accept_law_text_as_ruml_text includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/accept-law-text-as-ruml-text.ruml".

main is published at "eli/bund/bgbl-1/2003/s3023/2026-07-30/1/deu".

rule node_1 with provenance main at art-z1_abs-z_inhalt-n1_text-n1_marker-n1:
Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for a case if
    the answer to Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe for the case is a truth value
    and Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe would hold for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "accept-law-text-as-ruml-text.ruml" at generated_1:
    % no data
    node_1 expects answers ["Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

scenario generated_2 is, as stated in "accept-law-text-as-ruml-text.ruml" at generated_2:
    % every leaf answered yes
    the answer to Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe for case 1 is true.
    node_1 expects answers ["Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers [].

scenario generated_3 is, as stated in "accept-law-text-as-ruml-text.ruml" at generated_3:
    % the leaf 1 answered no, the others yes
    the answer to Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe for case 1 is false.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for case 1"].

scenario generated_4 is, as stated in "accept-law-text-as-ruml-text.ruml" at generated_4:
    % every leaf answered no
    the answer to Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe for case 1 is false.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for case 1"].

query node_1 is:
    Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for case 1.

query not_node_1 is:
    it is not the case that Aufgabe der Sozialhilfe holds for case 1.

